%T A399763 1957,112,282,622,4995,3130,1523,11727,1437,2201,8672,1566,1393,13355,
%U A399763 69506,26318,166630,165036,81004,11951,93498,8980,3521,342996,11610,9677,31296
%N A399763 a(n) = index of first appearance of a building of height n in the city-building sequence A399633, or -1 if no building has height n.
%C A399763 It is not known if every number is the height of some building. 56 is the smallest unseen height in the first 2.3 billion terms of A399633, thus this sequence is positive at least through a(55).
%H A399763 Eric Fox, <a href="/A399763/b399763.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..55</a>
%F A399763 a(n) = min{h >= 1: A399633(h) = n}.
%e A399763 a(8) = 1278 because 1278 is the earliest index n such that A399633(n) = 8.
%Y A399763 Left inverse of A399633.
